  "reason": "Grammar-input patch 0001 (upstream issue airbus-cert/tree-sitter-powershell#70) widens the ASCII-only name patterns of variables, command parameters, simple names and type identifiers to Unicode letters, decimal digits and underscore, so non-ASCII (for example Hangul) variable, parameter, hash-key, member and type names parse. Statement labels are not widened. Each listed difference is a patch-corpus input or its seeded edit in which such a name now parses, or in which a variable in an expandable string or here-string now spans non-ASCII letters; the pinned upstream corpus, its seeded edits, the kit inputs, the pinned large input and the Hangul statement-label corpus case are unchanged.",
  "retireWhen": "Retire with the matching patch when the upstream pin incorporates the fix; review anew for any identity, fixture or result change.",
